 ],
 "method_note": "Chernozhukov et al. (2018) partially linear DML: LightGBM learns E[y|controls] and E[momentum|controls] out of fold (purged date blocks), and theta is the slope of the residualized return on residualized momentum, with date-clustered errors. Compared with the naive OLS slope: if theta shrinks, part of 'momentum' was size / value / volatility exposure. Caveat: the universe is today's constituents (membership history starts 2026-10), so early years carry survivorship bias; read the premium as an upper bound.",
